"""qq — the quintessence CLI dispatcher (the strangler front door).

This is the FRONT DOOR — and since P9 (the release-gate legacy port) the WHOLE door: the read
verbs (menu/digest/findings/list/show/brief/path/help), the check-family verbs
(check/reconcile/waveoff), the write path's verbs (update/essence/new/rewrite/
finalize/checkpoint/save, + compact/delete/rm/reindex, P9), and the setup/diagnostic
trio (doctor/config/init -> quintessence.admin, P9) are all rendered natively by
quintessence.cli / quintessence.write / quintessence.admin on top of the package's L0/L1/L2
objects. `search`/`ask` are direct-exec'd straight to `qq-search`/`qq-ask` — see
`_DIRECT_EXEC`'s comment for the grounded env-leak bug behind that shape (historical: the
bootstrap it dodged was qq-legacy's, but the direct-exec is the right shape regardless).

The original all-bash engine (`qq-legacy`, plus the standalone `qq-write` binary) served as
the strangler host and whole-engine rollback throughout the port; both were purged from the
tree when the port completed (P9) and live in git history. The store format and the `.qq.lock`
discipline are unchanged, so any historical engine from git history still interoperates.
"""
